// The Hollow Hood (boss id hood): the journal, every hero in their own voice (docs/plans/journal-voices.md).
// Move keys are cast names (the journal fires on the cast bar's name); follow-up casts (Echo, Shatter, Last Toll, Rimeburst, Hollow Echo, Weighing, Calm Breaks, Burial) are covered by their pattern's page.
// The heroes only say what they saw: a figure in a torn coat, an empty hood with two cold slits, a blade in one hand and a light in the other.
(window.JOURNAL_DATA = window.JOURNAL_DATA || {}).hood = {
  meet: {
    bastion: "A tall, lean figure in a torn black coat stood in the middle of a frozen court, chains at its collar and nothing in its hood but two cold blue slits. Letters lay in the frost between us. Its hands were bare. I watched them, since the ground told me nothing.",
    gloomsworn: "Something tall and thin stood in the frozen court in a torn black coat, with chains at its collar and nothing in its hood but two blue slits. I have met the dead. This was emptier. Its hands hung open, and I watched them.",
    thresher: "Such a tall, thin guest, dear, in a torn black coat with chains at his collar and nothing in his hood but two cold blue lamps. Letters lie in the frost like dropped cards. His hands were empty, and I hummed, and he did not mind.",
    bloodreaver: "A tall thin cold one in a torn black coat, hood empty but two blue slits, chains at its neck! Letters in the frost at my feet. Hands bare. I want to see what it does with them. A good scar waiting, I can feel it.",
    runeguard: "The Hood: a tall figure in a torn black coat, chains at the collar, a hood with nothing in it but two cold slits of blue. Letters lie in the frost like marginalia. Its hands were bare, and the hands, I think, are the sign.",
    gorgemaw: "A new host: tall and thin, in a torn black coat, chains at the collar and a hood with nothing in it but two cold blue slits, in a court that smelled of ice. The letters in the frost were the menu, I assume. His hands were bare. I watched them like a waiter.",
    oathbroker: "The counterparty is tall and thin, in a torn black coat, with chains at its collar and nothing in its hood but two cold blue slits. Letters lie in the frost like a document torn up. Its hands are empty, and I suspect the terms are in the hands.",
    ironpalm: "It was tall, and thin, in a torn black coat. Chains at its collar. In its hood, nothing but two cold blue slits. Letters lay in the frost. Its hands were open and empty. I listened, and it said nothing yet.",
    ranger: "Tall. Lean. Torn black coat, chains at the collar, and a hood with nothing in it but two cold blue slits. Letters lying in the frost. Hands empty. Watched them from the south wall. They tell you everything.",
    shadowblade: "The mark is tall and thin, in a torn black coat with chains at its collar and a hood with nothing in it but two cold blue slits. Letters lie in the frost around us. Its hands were empty, and I wondered which would be raised first.",
    pyromancer: "An ICICLE in a torn black coat! Tall, thin, chains at its collar and two cold blue slits where a face should be, in a court full of frost and dropped letters. Hands empty. I could not decide whether I was insulted or intrigued.",
    thermist: "Cold: a tall thin shape in a torn black coat, chains at the collar, nothing in the hood but two blue slits, letters in the frost. Hands empty. Then it all rushed in, the cold of the court on my skin, and I ran cold all night.",
    driftblade: "Something tall and thin stood in the frozen court in a torn black coat with chains at its collar and nothing in its hood but two cold blue slits, and letters lay in the frost all round, and its hands were empty, and I circled it twice to see which would move first.",
    alembist: "Specimen: tall, thin, in a torn black coat; chains at the collar; a hood with nothing in it but two cold blue slits. Observed: letters lying in the frost, and hands that stay empty until they are not. Label: watch the hands. Two lanterns dropped, both accidental.",
    threadweaver: "A tall, thin thing in a torn black coat. Torn, mind, not mended. Chains at the collar, nothing in the hood but two cold blue slits, and letters dropped in the frost like loose buttons. Its hands were bare. I watched them for the first stitch.",
    marionettist: "A new star: tall, thin, in a torn black coat; chains at the collar; a hood with nothing in it but two cold blue slits, upstage in a frozen house strewn with letters. His hands were bare. A good actor keeps his hands still until the cue. (The Doll was unsettled.)",
    cleric: "A tall, thin figure in a torn black coat, chains at its collar and nothing in its hood but two cold blue lights. Letters lay in the frost, so many, like fallen petals. Its hands were empty. I prayed over it before I knew why.",
    grovekeeper: "Like the first deep frost of the year, tall and thin and quiet, in a torn black coat with chains at its collar and nothing in its hood but two blue slits. Letters lay in the frost like dropped seeds. Its hands were empty. I watched them, as you watch the sky.",
    chronomancer: "It was tall and thin, in a torn black coat, chains at the collar, nothing in the hood but two cold blue slits, and letters lying in the frost like dropped notes. Its hands are empty. They were empty. I was waiting for the beat they would stop being.",
    tidecaller: "A tall, thin figure stood in the frozen court like a standing stone at low water, in a torn black coat, chains at its collar, nothing in its hood but two cold blue slits. Letters lay in the frost like shells left by the ebb. Its hands were empty.",
    lanternkeeper: "A long dark draught in the shape of a tall thin person: torn black coat, chains at the collar, nothing in the hood but two cold blue slits. Letters lay in the frost. Its hands were empty. I lit a lamp for each of us, and kept my eye on the hands.",
    kenseier: "A tall figure, thin as a sword, in a torn black coat. Chains at the collar, and nothing in the hood but two cold blue slits. Letters lay in the frost. Its hands were empty, and I counted: a blow with no hands has no beat yet.",
    houndmaster: "Tall, lean thing in a torn black coat. Chains at the collar. Hood empty but for two cold blue slits. Letters in the frost, like dropped playing cards. Hands bare. Kept Rust and Ash close and watched the hands.",
  },
  win: {
    bastion: "The hooded one went down on one knee in the frost and stayed there, blade point to the floor, the light in its palm gone out. The chains hung slack. We were on our feet at the end, every one of us.",
    gloomsworn: "It knelt in the frost and the light in its palm went out. The chains stopped swinging. I have seen men set a post down before. The watch is relieved.",
    thresher: "He knelt in the frost, dear, and the light in his palm went out like a candle at the end of a party. The chains hung quiet. His hour was kept at last, and so, I think, was everyone's.",
    bloodreaver: "Down! It knelt in the frost, the light in its palm gone out, the blade point-down, and I was bleeding fine and proud. A scar for every window. Well fought, all of you.",
    runeguard: "The Hood knelt in the frost, blade point-down, the light in its palm gone out; the chains hung still. Every omen met in its order, and entered in the margin.",
    gorgemaw: "My host knelt in the frost, blade lowered, the light in his palm out. A cold meal, and slow, but a proper one, and the plates were cleared. I could have eaten another.",
    oathbroker: "The counterparty knelt in the frost, blade lowered, the light in its palm extinguished; the chains hang still. All terms discharged, none contested.",
    ironpalm: "It knelt in the frost. The blade lowered. The light in its palm went out, and the chains hung still. It had asked a great many questions, and we had answered every one.",
    ranger: "Down on one knee. Blade point-down. The light in its other hand out. Chains hanging still. Long trail, no wasted shots, and nothing left to follow.",
    shadowblade: "The mark knelt in the frost, blade point-down, the light in its palm gone out, the chains hanging still. It had never looked at us so closely as when it knelt.",
    pyromancer: "The icicle knelt! Blade down, the light in its palm out, the chains hanging quiet. I would like it noted that the court is warmer now, entirely thanks to me. Magnificent work, all of us.",
    thermist: "It knelt. Blade down, the light in its palm out, the chains still. The court felt warmer and I breathed out all of it at once. A cold ending. Quiet.",
    driftblade: "It knelt in the frost, blade lowered, the light in its palm out, the chains hanging still, and for the first time all night I had nothing to run round, so I stood still and did not hate it.",
    alembist: "Specimen kneeling in the frost, blade lowered, the light in its palm out, chains still. Observed: the court got a little warmer. Conclusion: well preserved, but over.",
    threadweaver: "It knelt in the frost, blade lowered, the light in its palm gone out, and the chains went slack. No thread left to pull. Rest your needles, my little stitches; it's over.",
    marionettist: "Curtain: the star knelt in the frost, blade lowered, the light in his palm out, the chains still. (The Doll took the bow.)",
    cleric: "It knelt in the frost, the blade lowered and the light in its palm gone out, and the chains hung still. I could not help but whisper a blessing. A quiet ending, and I am grateful for it.",
    grovekeeper: "The winter knelt at last, blade lowered, and the light in its palm went out. The chains hung quiet. I felt the court warm a little, the way a field does when the frost lifts.",
    chronomancer: "It knelt in the frost, the blade lowered, the light in its palm gone out, the chains finally quiet. I will have seen this before; I have not. It was good to hear it end on a held note.",
    tidecaller: "It knelt in the frost at last, the blade lowered and the light in its palm gone out, and the chains hung as still as a calm morning. The tide had turned in the court, and I felt it go out.",
    lanternkeeper: "It knelt in the frost, the blade lowered, and the light in its palm went out. The chains hung quiet. Four of us, four lamps, still burning, and one left on the step.",
    kenseier: "It knelt in the frost, the blade lowered, the light in its palm out. The chains hung still. It kept good time to the end, and the ash fell and was still.",
    houndmaster: "Down on one knee in the frost. Blade point-down, the light in its hand out, chains hanging still. Rust sat. Ash sat. We'll have him by supper.",
  },
  moves: {
    "Hollow Step": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "It walked at the nearest of us and swung twice. Light blows. I made sure I was always the nearest, so they landed on the shield and the line behind me was never chosen.",
      gloomsworn: "It walked to the nearest of us and swung twice, lightly. I stayed nearest. A wound is only a wound, and I had others behind me worth keeping clear of it.",
      thresher: "He walked to the nearest of us and swung twice, politely. I let our shield stay nearest and hummed on the far side of him. A tidy step keeps the hour away from the soft ones.",
      bloodreaver: "The cold one walked at the nearest of us and swung twice. Light! I kept myself nearest on purpose so the soft ones got none. Hardly a bruise, shameful.",
      runeguard: "It walked at the nearest of us with its hands empty, which is the sign. The shield stays nearest, so the two swings find the one prepared for them, and the rest of us keep clear.",
      gorgemaw: "My host walked at the nearest and swung twice. I stayed nearest, as a guest should be: closest to the plates. The swings landed on me, and the rest of the table ate in peace.",
      oathbroker: "The first clause is simple: it walks to the nearest and swings twice, payable by that party alone. I made myself the nearest, as is my right, and the rest of the party stayed behind me.",
      ironpalm: "It walked at the nearest and struck twice. Short words. I stayed nearest and answered each. The others stood behind and did not need to.",
      ranger: "It walked to the nearest of us and swung twice. Light. Our shield stayed nearest. The rest of us kept behind the shield and shot from there.",
      shadowblade: "The mark walked at the nearest of us and swung twice, which is dull of it. Our shield stayed nearest, and I stayed behind the shield, where nothing so crude ever reaches me.",
      pyromancer: "It walked at the nearest of us and swung twice, a perfectly ordinary insult. Our shield stayed nearest, and I stood far back and cast at it. Nothing in the world is safer.",
      thermist: "It walked at the nearest and swung twice. Slow. Our shield stayed nearest and took them, and the rest of us stayed behind and burned bright from there, hot and safe.",
      driftblade: "It walked at the nearest of us and swung twice, slowly, and our shield stayed nearest so the swings fell there, and I went round the back of it and out the other side, not once touching down.",
      alembist: "Complaint: it walks to the nearest and swings twice. Cure: keep the shield nearest, mend it from behind, and the rest of us stay where the swings cannot reach.",
      threadweaver: "It walked at the nearest and swung twice. I told our shield to stay nearest, and ran a thread to them first. The rest of my stitches stayed behind the seam. Watch the slack.",
      marionettist: "The star walked at the nearest of the company and swung twice. The shield took the front of the stage, and the rest of us kept the wings. (Exit the Doll, stage left, unharmed.)",
      cleric: "It walked to the nearest of us and swung twice. I asked our knight to stay nearest, and laid a little light on him before each swing instead of after. He barely staggered.",
      grovekeeper: "It walked to the nearest of us and swung twice, slow as weather. Our shield stayed nearest, rooted. The rest of my lot stood behind, and I had planted on the shield before the first swing.",
      chronomancer: "It walked at the nearest of us and swung twice, on the beats. Our shield stood nearest, so the swings landed there. I will have mended it before the second one. I did.",
      tidecaller: "It walked at the nearest of us and swung twice, a small slow swell. Our shield stayed nearest, so the swells broke on the shield, and the rest of us kept behind, on dry shingle.",
      lanternkeeper: "It walked at the nearest and swung twice. I hung a lantern on our shield beforehand, and the shield stayed nearest. The rest of us stayed behind, in the lit side.",
      kenseier: "It walked at the nearest and swung twice, on two honest beats. I stayed nearest and met each stroke with the blade as it landed. The others kept behind me and well off the line.",
      houndmaster: "The big lad walked at the nearest and swung twice. Stayed behind the shield-man. Let him have the front.",
    } },
    "Cold Breath": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A cone of cold came for the nearest, which was me. I took it on the shield, square. The others kept out of the cone's edge, and our healer saw to the chill after.",
      gloomsworn: "A cone of cold came at the nearest. Me. I drew the dark in and let it land. The rest stood out of its edge and the healer mended what it left.",
      thresher: "A little cone of cold for whoever was nearest, which was our shield, bless him. The rest of us stepped out of its edge, and our healer tucked the chill away after.",
      bloodreaver: "A cone of cold for the nearest, which was me. I took it full in the face and let it land. The others stood clear of the edge and the healer mended what was left of me.",
      runeguard: "A cone drawn at the nearest, whose ward is already laid. The rest of us stepped from its edge, and the chill it left was mended after. A modest cold, and well ordered.",
      gorgemaw: "A cone of cold, served to the nearest, which was me. I opened wide and took it square. The others stood to the side of the course and the healer mended the chill after. A modest dish.",
      oathbroker: "The cone is drawn on the floor before it is served, and payable by the nearest. I accepted delivery in full. The others stood outside its edge, and the healer settled the chill afterward.",
      ironpalm: "A cone of cold spoke to the nearest. I took it, whole. The others stood out of its edge, and the healer mended what it left.",
      ranger: "A cone aimed at the nearest. I was to the east of it, out of the arc. The chill it left was the healer's to mend.",
      shadowblade: "A cone for the nearest, and our shield took it. I stood at the edge and out of its arc. The healer mended the chill. It aimed at the wrong person, poor thing.",
      pyromancer: "A cone of frost at the nearest, our shield, thank goodness. I kept to the side, out of the arc, and cast on. The healer mended the chill afterward.",
      thermist: "Cone of cold at the nearest. Our shield took it. I stepped out of the edge, fast, and the rest followed, and the healer thawed what it left.",
      driftblade: "A cone of cold came for the nearest, our shield, and I swept out wide of its edge and round and in again behind it, while the healer mended the chill.",
      alembist: "Note: a cone of cold at the nearest. Our shield took it square; the rest of us stood out of the edge. A small chill, mended after. Nothing exploded.",
      threadweaver: "A cone of cold at the nearest. Our shield took it square and the rest of us stood clear of its edge. I mended the chill after, a tidy hem.",
      marionettist: "A cone of cold aimed at the front of the stage, where our shield stood. The company stepped out of its edge, and the healer mended the chill in the wings.",
      cleric: "A cone of cold at the nearest, and our knight took it, as he does. The rest of us stood to the side, and I mended the chill at once. Gently done.",
      grovekeeper: "A cone of cold came at the nearest, like a cold wind through a gap. The shield took it; the rest of us stood out of its edge. I mended the chill after, as you thaw a frost-bitten stem.",
      chronomancer: "A cone of cold at the nearest, on the downbeat. Our shield took it, the rest of us stood out of its edge, and I undid the chill after. It is easier when I have already done it.",
      tidecaller: "A cone of cold, a squall aimed at the nearest. Our shield took it, and the rest of us stood out of its edge. I brought the water up after, and the chill went out of them.",
      lanternkeeper: "A cone of cold at the nearest. I'd lit our shield already, and the rest stood out of the edge. One mend after, and the glow came back.",
      kenseier: "A cone of cold at the nearest. Not a stroke a blade can turn. I took it, and the others stood out of the edge. The healer mended the chill after the beat.",
      houndmaster: "Cold cone at the nearest. The shield-man took it. Dogs and I stood out of the edge. The healer mended the chill. Steady, lads.",
    } },
    "Frostfall": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Frost circles on the three furthest, never the nearest. Each of them stepped clear as the circle showed. I stayed close to it, and my ground stayed mine.",
      gloomsworn: "Frost circles fell on the three furthest from it, none on me. Each of them walked out of theirs as it showed on the floor. Standing close has its uses.",
      thresher: "Three rings of frost for the three of us furthest. The nearest is never asked. We each stepped out of ours as it was drawn, quite cheerfully.",
      bloodreaver: "Frost circles on the three furthest from it, never on me. Each of them stepped out as it was drawn. I felt left out, and stood closer.",
      runeguard: "Three rings of frost on the three furthest, never the nearest; that much is a pattern. Each of us stepped from the ring as it was drawn.",
      gorgemaw: "Three small rings of frost for the three furthest guests. Each stepped away from theirs as it was drawn. I was nearest, and was not asked, and took offence.",
      oathbroker: "Three small rings of frost, payable by the three furthest. Each party stepped clear of their own as it was drawn. The nearest is exempt, and I took the exemption.",
      ironpalm: "Three rings of frost, spoken to the three furthest. Each of us left ours as it was drawn. The nearest was not asked.",
      ranger: "Three frost rings dropped on the three furthest from it. Never the nearest. Stepped out west as mine was drawn and drew again from the new spot.",
      shadowblade: "Three rings of frost for the three furthest. I was one, and stepped out of mine as it was drawn, politely, and was nowhere near it when it landed.",
      pyromancer: "Three circles of frost on the three furthest from it, and I was one of them! I resented moving, then did it, and finished from the new place. It was the right call.",
      thermist: "Three rings of frost on the three furthest, and I was one, and I ran out of it hot and fast the instant it was drawn! The nearest was never asked. Calm again after.",
      driftblade: "Three rings of frost fell on the three furthest from it, and I was one, and I went out of mine the instant it was drawn and through the gap and round, quite pleased.",
      alembist: "Three rings of frost on the three furthest from it. I labelled mine and stepped out when it showed on the floor. The nearest was never dosed.",
      threadweaver: "Three rings of frost on the three furthest from it. Each stepped out as it was drawn. A sloppy seam would have stayed in the ring.",
      marionettist: "Three rings of frost for the three furthest from the star, upstage. We each left our mark as it was drawn. The front row was spared, as it always is.",
      cleric: "Three rings of frost fell on the three furthest from it. Each of my lambs stepped out as soon as it was drawn, and I stood well clear of mine, a little proud of them.",
      grovekeeper: "Three rings of frost came down on the three furthest, like early hail. Each of us stepped out as it was drawn. The nearest was never asked.",
      chronomancer: "Three rings of frost on the three furthest, all on one beat. We stepped out as they were drawn, and I stepped out a moment before I decided to. The nearest was never asked.",
      tidecaller: "Three rings of frost on the three furthest, small cold pools on the shore. We each stepped out as they were drawn, without hurry. The nearest was never asked.",
      lanternkeeper: "Three rings of frost on the three furthest from it. Each of us stepped out as the ring was drawn. Three rings, three of us, and one lit spot left for the nearest.",
      kenseier: "Three rings of frost, drawn on the three furthest. Each stepped out on the drawing. The nearest was never asked, and I stayed there.",
      houndmaster: "Three rings of frost on the three furthest from him. Walked out of mine as it was drawn. Rust would have sat in it, silly lad.",
    } },
    "Pale Waltz": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Four beats, each shown on the floor first. The cones and the circle were for the others to step from. I stayed hard at its feet, in the quiet middle of the ring, and the ring passed round me. The last blow came for everyone; I braced.",
      gloomsworn: "Four blows, each drawn first. The cones and the circle were meant for the living; I stayed at its feet in the ring's quiet middle, where I always am. The last blow touched everyone. I was dead for a few like that.",
      thresher: "A waltz in four steps, dear, and the floor shows each before it comes: a cone, a circle, a cone, and a ring about his feet. Whoever it points at steps off the mark. Stay snug against him or well outside the ring.",
      bloodreaver: "Four beats! Cone, circle, cone, then a ring round its feet. The others stepped away from the cones. I stayed right in its face, inside the ring, where the floor was quiet. The last one reached everyone. A proper one.",
      runeguard: "Four beats, in order, each drawn upon the floor before it falls: cone, circle, cone, and a ring about its feet. Step from the cone or circle meant for you; for the ring, stand within its quiet centre or well beyond. The last beat is for all.",
      gorgemaw: "A four-course service: cone, circle, cone, then a ring set round his feet. We left the first three plates for their owners and I kept my seat close in, inside the ring. The last course was served to every guest.",
      oathbroker: "Four instalments, in a fixed order: a cone, a circle, a cone, and a ring at its feet. Each was drawn on the floor before it fell, and the named party stepped aside. I took the ring's quiet centre, as the nearest. The final instalment fell on all of us alike.",
      ironpalm: "Four words. A cone. A circle. Another cone. A ring about its feet. Each was shown first. I answered by stillness, close in, in the ring's quiet middle. The last word was for everyone.",
      ranger: "Four beats. Cone, circle, cone, ring. Slid off the lines of the cones, held wide of the ring on the east side. The last blow reached everyone.",
      shadowblade: "Four beats, and the floor announced each. Cones and a circle are for those named, and I simply wasn't there. The ring I took from close in, under its chin. The last blow reached everyone, which was vulgar.",
      pyromancer: "Four beats, each glowing on the floor first: cone, circle, cone, and a ring about its feet! I stepped off the cones, stood close in for the ring, and finished my spell from there. The last blow reached everyone.",
      thermist: "Cold: cone, circle, cone, ring. Step off the cones. Then the heat rushed in, the ring about its feet, and I was already tight against it, in the quiet middle, burning. The last blow reached everyone, and I ran hot a long while after.",
      driftblade: "Four beats and I ran every one: out of the cone aimed at me, round the cone aimed at the other, clear of the circle on the healer, and in close to its feet to wait out the ring, which I hated, and then the last blow reached us all.",
      alembist: "Compound of four doses, in fixed order: cone, circle, cone, ring. Doses one and three go to named patients, who step out of the flask's reach. Stay corked close to it for the ring. The final dose reaches the whole shelf.",
      threadweaver: "Four stitches in a fixed order, drawn on the floor first: cone, circle, cone, then a ring round its feet. Snip yourself out of the first three. For the ring, hug the seam close or stay well outside. The final stitch pulled the entire seam.",
      marionettist: "A waltz in four beats, as the playbill says: cone, circle, cone, and a ring about his feet. The company stepped out of the first three on cue and I kept my Doll in the wings. For the finale we stood snug against the star or well downstage. The last bow took us all.",
      cleric: "Four beats, and each was drawn on the floor before it fell, which I thought considerate. The cone and the circle I asked my young ones to step from; the ring we met close in or well outside. The last blow touched us all.",
      grovekeeper: "Four beats rolled in like a front, each marked on the floor: cone, circle, cone, then a ring about its feet. Step from the first three. For the ring, stand right in at its roots, or well out. The last beat touched everyone.",
      chronomancer: "A waltz in four beats: cone, circle, cone, ring about its feet. I stepped off the cone just before it landed, which is the whole trick. For the ring, close in or far out. The last beat touched everyone. I think I knew the tempo all along.",
      tidecaller: "Four swells, each showing on the floor like a shadow under water: cone, circle, cone, and a ring about its feet. We moved off the first three as they rose, and I kept to the still water close in for the ring. The last swell reached the whole shore.",
      lanternkeeper: "Four beats, drawn on the floor before each fell: cone, circle, cone, and a ring about its feet. I lit the way out of each for whoever it named, and stood close in for the ring, inside its quiet. The last beat reached all four lamps.",
      kenseier: "Four beats, laid out on the floor before each: cone, circle, cone, a ring about its feet. We stepped off the first three on their count. The last beat was for everyone, and no blade turns it.",
      houndmaster: "Four beats: cone at one of us, circle on the healer, cone at the other, a ring round his feet. Stepped out of the cones. For the ring I stood in tight against him, dogs at my heels. The last one reached the lot of us.",
    } },
    "Severance": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The blade meant the strikers were hunted. I took the ground between the dash and one of them, and it ended on my shield; the freeze left me quickly. The other would take the echo, so our healer had them mended first.",
      gloomsworn: "The blade came out, and two of the living were lined. I put myself between the dash and one of them, and it ended on me. The cold passed. The other was mended before the echo.",
      thresher: "The blade slid out and two of us were pointed at. Our shield stepped in front of one line, and he thaws in half the time, bless him. The other we kept brimming before the echo came down.",
      bloodreaver: "Blade out and two hitters lined! I threw myself between the dash and one of them and let it break on my chest. Froze a moment, grinned. The other got mended before the echo.",
      runeguard: "The blade is the sign: the strikers will be hunted. I set my ward between the dash and one of them, and it broke on the ward. The other, frozen, was mended above the echo.",
      gorgemaw: "The blade came out and two guests were singled out. I put my chest in front of one dash and swallowed it whole; the freeze was gone before the next course. The other guest was topped up before the echo arrived.",
      oathbroker: "The blade drawn, two strikers named. I interposed between the dash and one of them, and the debt stopped at my shield. The other was provisioned for the echo before it was called in.",
      ironpalm: "The blade came out. It asked two strikers. I put my open hand between the dash and one of them, and the question ended there. The other was mended before the echo.",
      ranger: "Blade out. Two of us on the wall were lined. Our shield took one line square. Mine I took, froze, and was topped up before the echo.",
      shadowblade: "The blade came out and two of us were lined up, how flattering. Our shield stood in one line and the dash died on him. Mine found me, froze me, and I was mended before the echo.",
      pyromancer: "The blade came out, two of us lined! Our shield stood in front of one dash and it died on him. I took mine, froze like a candle in a cellar, and was mended before the echo.",
      thermist: "Blade out, and two of us were lined. Our shield took one dash and thawed quickly. Mine took me, and I ran cold until the healer's warmth reached me, before the echo fell.",
      driftblade: "The blade came out and two of us were lined, and our shield stepped into the line so the dash stopped on him, while mine caught me, froze me, thawed me, and I was mended before the echo came down.",
      alembist: "Blade drawn means the strikers are the patients. Our shield took one dash as a stopper would; I measured the other a full mend before the echo came due.",
      threadweaver: "The blade came out and my two needles were lined. Our shield stood in front of one, so the dash caught on his seam, and I mended the other above the echo before it came down. A neat piece of work.",
      marionettist: "The blade came out, and two of the cast were lined. The shield stood in one line, and the dash stopped on him. My own I took, frozen, thawed and mended before the echo. (My Doll stood well back.)",
      cleric: "The blade came out, two of the young ones lined. Our knight stood in front of one dash, and he thaws quickly, bless him. The other I mended before the echo ever reached them.",
      grovekeeper: "The blade came out, two of the strikers lined like saplings in a gale. Our shield stood before one, and the dash stopped there. The other I mended deep, before the echo broke over them.",
      chronomancer: "The blade came out and two of us were lined, with the echo to follow. Our shield stood before one dash. The other I mended early, before the echo, which is when it counts.",
      tidecaller: "The blade came out and two of the strikers were lined, like two boats in a rip. Our shield put himself in front of one, and the dash broke on him. The other I filled with water before the echo came back down.",
      lanternkeeper: "The blade came out, two strikers lined. I hung a light on our shield, and they stood in one line, so the dash stopped there. The other I mended before the echo, a long breath ahead of it.",
      kenseier: "A blade out means the strikers are named. I stepped into one line and met the dash as it landed, and it stopped. A short freeze, a quick thaw. The other was mended before the echo.",
      houndmaster: "Blade out, two of us on a lead. The shield-man stood in front of one dash and it stopped on him. Mine took me, froze me, thawed. The healer had me topped up before the echo.",
    } },
    "Hollow Procession": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Three figures at the wall. I looked for lit eyes and a drawn blade and put myself in front of whichever of us that one chose. The others only sting. The real dash freezes, and the shatter after finds the frozen.",
      gloomsworn: "Three hooded shapes at the wall. One had lit eyes and a drawn blade. I took its line. The rest were shadows of it and sting like shadows. The true one freezes, and the shatter after goes looking for whoever froze.",
      thresher: "Three hooded guests along the wall, but only one with bright eyes and the blade drawn. Our shield found him, dear, and took the line. The others only tap on the shoulder. His dash chills, and the shatter finds whoever is chilled.",
      bloodreaver: "Three of them along the wall! Only one had lit eyes and the blade drawn. I stood in front of whoever that one chose, my friend. The copies just sting. The true one freezes, and the shatter finds whoever's frozen.",
      runeguard: "Three hooded figures at the wall; only one has lit eyes and the blade drawn. I placed myself in that line. The copies do little. The true dash freezes, and the shatter that follows seeks the frozen.",
      gorgemaw: "Three hooded waiters along the wall, but only one with lit eyes and the blade drawn. I stood where that one was sending its dash. The rest are garnish. The true course freezes, and the shatter goes for whoever is frozen.",
      oathbroker: "Three hooded signatories at the wall; only one with bright eyes and the blade drawn. I stood in that line. The copies' payments are minor. The true dash freezes, and the shatter that follows is levied on whoever is frozen.",
      ironpalm: "Three figures at the wall, three questions. One had lit eyes and a drawn blade. I answered that one. The copies spoke softly. The true one froze, and the shatter that followed found the frozen.",
      ranger: "Three figures at the wall. Only one had lit eyes and a blade out. Our shield stood in that line. The others only tap. The true dash freezes, and the shatter finds the frozen.",
      shadowblade: "Three hooded figures at the wall, one with lit eyes and the blade drawn: the only one worth noticing. Our shield took its line. The rest only sting. The true dash freezes, and the shatter finds the frozen.",
      pyromancer: "Three icicles at the wall, and only one with lit eyes and a blade! Our shield stood in that line. The copies are a flick; the true one freezes, and the shatter after finds whoever is frozen.",
      thermist: "Three shapes at the wall, one with lit eyes. Cold clarity: that one carries the blade. Our shield stood in front of it. The false ones are flurries. The true dash froze whoever it caught, and the shatter went hunting for them.",
      driftblade: "Three shapes at the wall and one with lit eyes and a blade, and our shield read it and stood in its line, and the copies stung but the true dash froze and the shatter found whoever was frozen.",
      alembist: "Three hooded specimens along the wall, one with lit eyes and the blade: the genuine article. Our shield stood in its line. Counterfeits only sting. The genuine one freezes, and the shatter is dosed to whoever is frozen.",
      threadweaver: "Three hooded patches along the wall, one with lit eyes and the blade drawn. That is the true seam, so our shield took its line. The false ones snag but do not tear. The true one freezes, and the shatter finds whoever is frozen.",
      marionettist: "Three hooded players upstage and one with lit eyes and the blade: the lead. The shield took his line. The understudies only prick. The lead freezes, and the shatter finds whoever is frozen.",
      cleric: "Three hooded shapes at the wall, and only one with lit eyes and the blade drawn. I trusted our knight to know it, and he stood in its line. The others only sting. The true dash freezes, and the shatter finds the frozen.",
      grovekeeper: "Three hooded shapes at the wall, like three fogs, and only one with bright eyes and a blade. Our shield stood in that line. The others are a spring shower; the true one freezes, and the shatter finds the frozen.",
      chronomancer: "Three hooded shapes at the wall, rehearsing; only one had lit eyes and a drawn blade. Our shield took that one's line. The true dash freezes, and the shatter lands on the frozen, so that hero must be full by then.",
      tidecaller: "Three hooded shapes along the wall, three lines, and only one with bright eyes and a blade. Our shield stood in that line, and the copies broke on nothing. The true dash froze, and the shatter found whoever was frozen.",
      lanternkeeper: "Three hooded shapes at the wall, one with bright eyes and a drawn blade. I could tell it by its light. Our shield stood in that line. The others only sting. The true dash freezes, and the shatter finds whoever is frozen.",
      kenseier: "Three figures at the wall. One had lit eyes and a drawn blade. I read that one and stood in its line. The copies cost a sting. The true dash freezes, and the shatter finds whoever is frozen.",
      houndmaster: "Three hooded shapes at the wall. One had lit eyes and a blade out. The shield-man read it right, stood in its line. Copies only sting. The true dash freezes, and the shatter finds whoever froze.",
    } },
    "The Tolling": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Light over the healer meant the bell: three tolls and then a worse one. A blue ring stood beside them each time. I stood in that ring for each toll, and our healer mended in the gaps.",
      gloomsworn: "A lantern over the healer, then a bell, three tolls and a last one worse. A blue ring stood beside them every time. I took the tolls there. The dark was glad of the work.",
      thresher: "A lantern over our healer and a bell for three tolls, with a last one that was not polite. Each toll had a blue ring beside the healer. One of us stepped in for the toll, and the healer mended the gaps.",
      bloodreaver: "Lantern over the healer, then the bell, three tolls and a worse one, and a blue ring at the healer's side each time. I stood in it and took the lot! Honest cold blows. The healer mended the gaps.",
      runeguard: "The light is the sign for the healer. A lantern, a bell for three tolls and a worse fourth, and a blue ring at the healer's side for each. I took the tolls in that ring; the healer mended between them.",
      gorgemaw: "A lantern over the healer and a bell, three tolls and a nasty one after. Beside the healer, a blue ring each time. I sat in it and took the tolls, which are cold dishes, and the healer mended in the pauses.",
      oathbroker: "A lantern over the healer, a bell for three tolls and a heavier fourth, and a blue ring as surety beside the healer for each. I stood in it for the tolls, and the healer settled between them.",
      ironpalm: "A lantern over the healer, and the bell. Three tolls, and a heavier. A blue ring at the healer's side each time. I stood in it and listened. The healer mended between.",
      ranger: "Lantern over the healer. A bell, three tolls and a worse fourth. A blue ring at the healer's side each time. Stepped in for a toll, then back to the line.",
      shadowblade: "A lantern over the healer, a bell for three tolls and a rude fourth, and a blue ring at the healer's side each time. I stepped into the ring and took one, unseen. The healer mended between.",
      pyromancer: "A lantern floated over the healer, outrageously, with a bell: three tolls, and a worse one. A blue ring glowed beside them each time. I strode in and took a toll myself, and the healer mended between.",
      thermist: "A lantern over the healer, a bell, three tolls and a worse one. I ran hot, stood in the blue ring at the healer's side and took a toll for them, cold to the bone. The healer mended the gaps.",
      driftblade: "A lantern over the healer and a bell tolling three times and once more, worse, and a blue ring beside the healer each time, and I hate standing still but I ran in and took a toll for them, and out again.",
      alembist: "Light over me, so a bell: three tolls and a bitter fourth. Beside me, a blue ring each time. One of the others stood in it and drank the toll for me, and I brewed in the gaps.",
      threadweaver: "A lantern hung over me, and the bell tolled three times, then a worse one. A blue ring beside me each time. One of my stitches stood in it for the toll, and I darned the gaps.",
      marionettist: "A lantern over the healer, a bell for three tolls and a nasty fourth, and a blue ring at the healer's side each time. I stepped into the spotlight and took one toll in their place. (Applause, thin.)",
      cleric: "A lantern hung over me and a bell tolled three times, and once more, worse. A blue ring stood beside me for each. One of my lambs stepped in and took the toll in my place, and I mended in between.",
      grovekeeper: "A lantern over me, and a bell for three tolls, like a hard rain, then one heavier. A blue ring beside me each time. One of my lot stood in it and took the toll, and I sowed the gaps.",
      chronomancer: "A lantern over me, and the bell tolling three times, then once more, out of time. A blue ring beside me on each toll. One of the others stood in it for the toll, and I filled the rests between.",
      tidecaller: "A lantern hung over me and a bell tolled three times, deep as a buoy, and once more heavily. A blue ring stood beside me each time. One of the others stepped into it for the toll. The water was high before the last.",
      lanternkeeper: "A lantern hung over me, and the bell tolled three times and a heavy fourth. A blue ring stood beside me each time. Three lights, four of us: one of the others stood in the ring for each toll. The lamps stayed warm.",
      kenseier: "Light over the healer: the bell, three tolls and a worse fourth, each on a beat I could count. A blue ring stood beside the healer at each. I stood in it and took the tolls. The healer mended in the rests.",
      houndmaster: "A lantern over the healer, three tolls and a worse one, a blue ring at the healer's side for each. Walked in and took a toll. Dogs stayed back of the ring. The healer mended in between.",
    } },
    "Pursuit": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "It chose one striker and a red circle trailed them. The striker kept moving; I took the circle on my shield the first time it landed. The hunt ended there.",
      gloomsworn: "It hunted one of the living. A red circle trailed them and locked and landed. They kept moving until the lock. I stood in the circle on the first landing, and that ended the hunt.",
      thresher: "He picked one of us and drew a red circle that followed, then locked, then landed. The one chosen kept dancing till the lock. Our shield stood in the circle, and the chase was over, tidy as you like.",
      bloodreaver: "It hunted one hitter, a red circle on their heels, locked and landed. They ran till the lock. I planted myself in the circle on the first landing and took it. A scar worth keeping.",
      runeguard: "The blade again, and one striker singled out: a red circle that follows, locks and lands, three times. The striker moved until each lock. I entered the circle at the first landing, and the hunt was ended.",
      gorgemaw: "He picked one striker for the chase: a red circle that followed, locked and landed. The striker kept moving; I sat down in the circle on the first landing and ate it, and the hunt ended. A dull dish, honestly.",
      oathbroker: "One striker was named in pursuit: a red circle that follows, locks and lands, three times. The striker moved until each lock. I entered the circle at the first landing and settled the sum, and the pursuit lapsed.",
      ironpalm: "It asked one striker, again and again. A red circle followed them, locked, landed. The striker walked on. At the first landing I stood in the circle, and it stopped asking.",
      ranger: "It hunted me. A red circle on my heels, locking, then landing, three times. Kept moving till each lock. Our shield took the circle on the first landing and the hunt ended there.",
      shadowblade: "It hunted me, a red circle at my heels, locking, then landing, three times. I kept to the dark between locks. Our shield stepped into the circle on the first landing and caught it. It looked everywhere but at me.",
      pyromancer: "It hunted me! A red circle on my heels that locked, then landed, three times. I ran in a fury until each lock. Our shield took the circle on the first landing, and that was the end of the chase.",
      thermist: "It hunted me. A red circle, locking, landing, three times. I ran hot and fast till each lock, and our shield stood in the circle on the first landing. The hunt stopped cold.",
      driftblade: "It hunted me, a red circle on my heels, locking and landing three times, and I ran round and round until each lock, and our shield walked into the circle and caught the first landing, so the chase ended without my having to stop once.",
      alembist: "One striker singled out: a red circle that follows, then locks, then lands, three times. The patient kept pacing until each lock. Our shield stepped into the circle for the first landing, and the experiment ended.",
      threadweaver: "One of my needles was singled out: a red circle that followed, locked and landed, three times. They kept moving, like thread through cloth, until each lock. Our shield took the first landing and cut the hunt short.",
      marionettist: "He chose me for the chase: a red circle trailing, locking, landing, three times. I kept in motion until each lock. The shield stood in the circle on the first landing, and the scene was cut short. (My Doll stayed in the wings.)",
      cleric: "It hunted one of the young ones: a red circle that followed, locked and landed, three times. The poor soul kept moving until each lock. Our knight stood in the circle and caught the first landing, and the hunt ended.",
      grovekeeper: "It hunted one striker, a red circle that followed, locked and landed, like a hailstorm that has chosen one field. The striker kept moving until each lock. Our shield took the first landing in the circle, and it was over.",
      chronomancer: "It hunted a striker, a red circle that followed, locked and landed, three times. The striker kept moving until each lock. Our shield took the first landing and the hunt ended early. It ends. It ended.",
      tidecaller: "It hunted a striker: a red circle that followed, locked and landed, three times. The striker kept moving, as a boat moves off a rock. Our shield stood in the circle for the first landing, and the hunt ended there.",
      lanternkeeper: "It hunted a striker, a red circle that followed, locked and landed, three times. The striker kept walking the long way round. Our shield stood in the circle on the first landing, and the hunt ended. One light on the shield.",
      kenseier: "The blade again. A red circle followed one striker, locked, and landed, three times. The striker moved until each lock. I stepped into the circle on the first landing and met it. The hunt ended.",
      houndmaster: "He hunted me. Red circle on my heels, locked, landed, three times. Kept running till each lock, like walking a dog round a post. The shield-man stood in the circle and the hunt stopped.",
    } },
    "Rimelight": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A beam of light ran through the healer from the open palm. Whoever stood first in it took the freeze. I stood first, nearest the palm. The burst that closed it went through all of us.",
      gloomsworn: "Light from its palm ran through the healer and pulsed. The first of us in it froze. That was me, by choice, nearest the hand. The burst after went through everyone, and I was already cold.",
      thresher: "A beam from his palm ran through the healer, pulsing. Whoever was first in it froze till the end, so our shield was first, dear, and warm again soon. The burst after reached the whole party.",
      bloodreaver: "A beam of light through the healer, three pulses. First one in it freezes to the end. Me, nearest the hand, on purpose. Then the burst, and everyone mended in one great breath.",
      runeguard: "Light from the palm ran through the healer, pulsing. Whoever stood first in it froze. I stood first, by design, nearest the hand. The burst that closed it reached all of us.",
      gorgemaw: "A beam of light from his palm through the healer, three pulses, freezing the first guest in it. I sat first, nearest the hand, and the rest behind me. The burst after went round the room, and was bland.",
      oathbroker: "A beam of light from its palm, through the healer, pulsing. The first party in it froze. I took first place, nearest the hand. The balance, the burst, fell on everyone, and we had provided for it.",
      ironpalm: "A beam of light from the palm through the healer. Pulses. The first of us in it was frozen. I stood first, nearest the hand. The burst afterwards spoke to everyone.",
      ranger: "Light from its palm through the healer, pulsing, freezing whoever stood first in it. Our shield stood first. I stayed behind. The burst after reached everyone.",
      shadowblade: "A beam of light through the healer, freezing the first one standing in it. Our shield stood first, nearest the hand. I stayed out of the light. The burst after found the whole room.",
      pyromancer: "A beam of light through the healer, freezing whoever stood first in it. Our shield stood first, nearest the hand, and I stood behind, glowing. The burst after reached all of us.",
      thermist: "Beam of light through the healer, three pulses, freezing the first of us in it. Our shield stood first, nearest the hand, and the rest of us behind. The burst after went through the lot of us. Level again.",
      driftblade: "A beam of light from its palm through the healer, three pulses, freezing the first of us in it, so our shield stood first, nearest the hand, and I ran round behind and the burst after found the whole court.",
      alembist: "Beam of light through me from its palm, three pulses; the first in it freezes. Our shield stood first. I stood behind, shelves in order, and the burst after reached all of us.",
      threadweaver: "A beam of light through me from its palm, three pulses, freezing whoever stood first in it. Our shield stood first. I kept behind. The burst after found all of us, mended.",
      marionettist: "A beam of light from his palm through the healer, three pulses, freezing the first of the company in it. The shield stood first, nearest the hand, and I directed from the back. The burst after reached the whole house.",
      cleric: "A beam of light ran through me from its palm, and froze whoever stood first in it. Our knight stood first, bless him, and I stayed behind him. The burst after found all of us, mended.",
      grovekeeper: "A beam of light ran from its palm through me, and froze whoever stood first in it. Our shield stood first, nearest the hand, and the burst after broke over all of us. I had planted beforehand.",
      chronomancer: "A beam of light through me, freezing the first of us in it. Our shield stood first, and thawed fastest. I stood back, out of the beam's rhythm, and the burst after found everyone mended.",
      tidecaller: "A beam of light ran through me from its palm, freezing the first of us in it. Our shield stood first, and thawed fastest, and I stood behind. The burst after found all of us with the water high.",
      lanternkeeper: "A beam of light ran from its palm through me, freezing the first of us in it. Our shield stood first, a lamp on their shoulder, and I stood behind. The burst after found all four of us lit.",
      kenseier: "A beam of light through the healer, three pulses, freezing whoever stood first in it. I stood first, nearest the hand. The burst after came a beat behind the last pulse and reached everyone.",
      houndmaster: "Beam of light through the healer, froze the first in it. The shield-man stood first, nearest the hand. Dogs behind him. The burst after found us all.",
    } },
    "Hollowing": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "All of us cut to a sliver at once, and a heavy blow behind. Nothing to take on the shield. Our healer filled us back above half in the gap, and the echo met a line that was still standing.",
      gloomsworn: "All of us cut to a sliver at once, and a heavy blow behind. Nothing to stand in front of. The healer filled us back above half in the gap, and that was all of the plan.",
      thresher: "All of us cut to a sliver at once, with a heavy blow trailing behind. Nothing to step out of. The healer filled us past half in the gap, and we took the echo together.",
      bloodreaver: "Everyone cut to a sliver, and a heavy blow behind! Nothing to strike at. I loved it and hated it. The healer filled us back above half in the gap.",
      runeguard: "Both hands: the sign for everyone. Each of us was cut to a sliver, and a heavy blow followed. Nothing to ward. The healer filled us above half in the gap.",
      gorgemaw: "Everyone cut to a sliver, and a heavy dish behind it. Nothing to push away. The healer filled each of us above half in the gap, and we cleared the echo together.",
      oathbroker: "A clause with no exemptions: every party reduced to a sliver, and a heavy payment due behind. The healer provided for each of us above half, and the echo was met.",
      ironpalm: "It spoke to everyone at once, and loudly. Each of us cut to a sliver, and a heavy word behind. The healer filled us above half in the gap, and we replied together.",
      ranger: "Everyone cut to a sliver, a heavy blow behind. No lane, no cover. Healer filled us back above half in the gap, and we took the echo together.",
      shadowblade: "Everyone cut to a sliver at once, a heavy blow behind it. No shadow deep enough. The healer filled us above half in the gap and the echo found us whole.",
      pyromancer: "Everyone cut to a sliver at once, a heavy blow behind it! Nothing to dodge and no one to blame. The healer filled us back above half in the gap, and I did not complain once.",
      thermist: "Everyone cut to a sliver at once, a heavy blow trailing behind. Nothing to dodge. Cold dread, then the healer's warmth; above half in the gap. We took the echo together.",
      driftblade: "Everyone was cut to a sliver at once with a heavy blow behind it and no way through, so I stood still, which I hate, and the healer filled us above half and the echo found us ready.",
      alembist: "Everyone cut to a sliver at once, a heavy dose behind. No dodging it. I mixed the mending for the quiet before; everyone above half in the gap, and the echo found us ready. One small fire, entirely planned.",
      threadweaver: "Everyone cut to a sliver at once, with a heavy blow in the gap behind it. No slack to take up. I tied each of my stitches back above half, and we took the echo together.",
      marionettist: "Everyone cut to a sliver at once, a heavy blow behind it, and no cue to miss. The healer filled the company above half in the gap and we took the echo together. (The Doll fainted prettily.)",
      cleric: "Every one of us was cut down to a sliver at once, and a heavy blow was coming behind. Nothing to stand in front of, dear hearts. I filled each of us back above half in the gap and we lived through the echo.",
      grovekeeper: "Everyone cut to a sliver at once, with a heavy blow behind like thunder behind lightning. I had planted early: all of us above half in the gap, and the echo found us ready.",
      chronomancer: "Everyone was cut to a sliver at once, and the heavy blow came in the gap behind it. There is nothing to dodge. I filled everyone above half in the gap, and we lived. Just.",
      tidecaller: "All of us cut down to a sliver, and a heavy blow behind it, as a second wave comes behind the first. I brought the water up in the gap, and we stood in the echo above half. It never needed hurry.",
      lanternkeeper: "Everyone was cut to a sliver at once, and a heavy blow behind. No corner to hide in. I topped up each wick in the gap, and we took the echo together, above half and burning.",
      kenseier: "Everyone cut to a sliver at once, and a heavy stroke behind it. A blade cannot turn it. The healer filled us above half in the rest between, and we stood in the echo together.",
      houndmaster: "Everyone cut to a sliver at once, heavy blow behind it. Nothing to run from. Whistled the dogs in beside the healer, got mended above half in the gap, and sat it out together.",
    } },
    "The Scales": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The floor split. Strikers belong on the light side, the healer on the blade side; I went where the healer went. Then it turned, and every one of us crossed again. Wrong side is ice.",
      gloomsworn: "The floor was split in two, one half the blade's and one the light's. The two who strike went to the light. The healer and I took the other half. Then it turned, and we all crossed again.",
      thresher: "The room divided into the blade's half and the light's, dear. The two who strike took the light; the healer and our shield took the blade. Then he turned it all about, and we swapped places like partners at a ball.",
      bloodreaver: "The floor split, half the blade's, half the light's. Hitters to the light, the healer to the blade half, and I went with the healer. Then it turned and we all ran across again. The wrong side was ice, and it bit.",
      runeguard: "The floor was divided: a half marked with the blade, a half with the light. Strikers to the light, healer to the blade half, I with the healer; then the halves turned and all crossed again. The wrong side is ice.",
      gorgemaw: "The floor was split like a seating plan, blade half and light half. The strikers sat in the light, the healer and I in the blade half. Then he turned the tables and we all changed seats. The wrong side was ice.",
      oathbroker: "The floor was divided into two jurisdictions, the blade's and the light's. Strikers belong to the light, the healer and I to the blade side. The terms were then reversed and every party crossed again. The wrong side is ice.",
      ironpalm: "The floor split. A half for the blade, a half for the light. Strikers crossed to the light. The healer and I took the blade half. It turned, and we crossed again.",
      ranger: "Wall split down the middle. One side blade, one side light. Mine was the light. Crossed on the turn, quick, nothing wasted. Wrong side is ice.",
      shadowblade: "The floor split, blade side and light side. Light for the knives, which pleased me; the healer and our shield on the blade side. It turned, we crossed. The wrong side was ice.",
      pyromancer: "The floor split in two: a blade half and a light half. Strikers to the light, naturally, where the glow is. The healer and our shield went to the blade half. Then it turned and we crossed again.",
      thermist: "Two halves: one drawn with the blade, one with the light. Cold fact: my kind belongs in the light. The healer and our shield took the blade half. Then it turned, and I ran flushed across the floor again.",
      driftblade: "The floor split, a blade half and a light half, and the strikers ran through to the light and the healer and our shield to the blade side, and then it turned and we ran across again, which was the only part I liked.",
      alembist: "The floor, divided like a double-chambered flask: blade side, light side. Strikers into the light, me and our shield into the blade side. Then the flask was turned over and everything crossed back. The wrong chamber is ice.",
      threadweaver: "The floor was cut in two like cloth: blade half, light half. My needles to the light, me and our shield to the blade half. Then it turned the cloth over and we crossed again. The wrong side frays into ice.",
      marionettist: "The stage split in two, a blade side and a light side. The cast who strike crossed to the light, the healer and shield to the blade side. Then he turned the stage and we crossed again. The wrong side was ice.",
      cleric: "The floor split in two, a half drawn with the blade and a half with the light. The young ones went to the light; I went to the blade half with our knight. Then it turned and we crossed again. The wrong side was ice.",
      grovekeeper: "The floor split in two, like a field in two seasons. The strikers went to the light and I to the blade half with our shield. Then it turned, and we all crossed over. The wrong side was ice.",
      chronomancer: "The floor divided, blade side and light side, and the strikers crossed to the light while I took the blade side with our shield. Then it turned, on the next bar, and we crossed again. The wrong side is ice.",
      tidecaller: "The floor split in two like a channel between banks, the blade's half and the light's. The strikers crossed to the light; the shield and I took the blade half. Then it turned and we crossed again.",
      lanternkeeper: "The floor split in two, a blade half and a light half. Strikers to the light; the shield and I to the blade half. Then it turned and we crossed again. I picked my lamp up and set it down on the other side.",
      kenseier: "The floor split in two, blade half and light half. Strikers to the light; the healer and I to the blade half. It turned after a long breath, and we all crossed again. The wrong side is ice.",
      houndmaster: "Floor split, blade half and light half. Sent my lot to the light, kept the healer and shield-man on the other. Then it turned and we crossed. Ice if you got it wrong.",
    } },
    "Dead Calm": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Eyes shut. Frost rings closed in on the strikers, and a cold patch opened under one. They stepped off it early, then froze where they stood. Anyone who shifted was cut. I kept my place and watched.",
      gloomsworn: "Its eyes shut, and the strikers had frost rings closing on them. A cold patch opened under one. They stepped off and then stood like the dead, which I recommend. Whoever moved was cut.",
      thresher: "His eyes closed, and the cold shrank around the two of us who strike. A frost patch opened under one, so off it, early, and then not a twitch. Whoever fidgeted was cut, and the heavy blow followed.",
      bloodreaver: "Eyes shut. Frost rings closed round the hitters, and a cold patch opened under one. Off it early, then stone. I don't love standing still, but moving got you cut, and I watched them do it right.",
      runeguard: "The eyes closed, and rings of frost narrowed upon the strikers. A cold patch opened beneath one. They stepped off it early and held perfectly still; any who moved was cut, and the heavy blow came for them.",
      gorgemaw: "His eyes closed, and frost rings drew round the strikers. A cold patch opened under one. They left it early and then sat quite still, as one does when the souffle is rising. Whoever moved was cut.",
      oathbroker: "Its eyes closed, rings of frost narrowed on the strikers, and a cold patch opened under one. They quit it early and then stood entirely still. Any who moved was cut, and the penalty followed.",
      ironpalm: "Its eyes closed. Rings of frost narrowed on the strikers. A cold patch opened under one. They left it, early, then were silent in the feet. Whoever spoke with a step was cut.",
      ranger: "Eyes shut. Rings of frost drawing in on the two of us. A cold patch under one. Stepped off, early, then stood stock still, like a deer. Anyone who moved was cut.",
      shadowblade: "Its eyes closed, and rings of frost drew in on the two of us. A cold patch under one. Off it early, then utterly still, as I have been in a hundred wardrobes. Whoever moved was cut.",
      pyromancer: "Its eyes shut and frost rings drew in on us. A cold patch opened under me. I stepped off, grumbled, then stood perfectly still, which I find unbearable. Anyone who moved was cut.",
      thermist: "Its eyes shut and frost rings tightened on me. A cold patch opened under my feet. Off it, hot with annoyance, and then still. Perfectly, coldly still. Whoever moved was cut.",
      driftblade: "Its eyes closed and rings of frost drew in on us and a cold patch opened under me, so I ran off it early, round it, and then had to stop, dead still, which I would not wish on anyone, and anyone who moved was cut.",
      alembist: "Eyes closed. Rings of frost narrowed on the strikers, a cold patch bloomed under one. Step off, early; then hold still as a sealed jar. Whoever twitched was cut and dosed again.",
      threadweaver: "Eyes closed, frost rings drew tight round my two needles. A cold patch opened under one. Off it early, then not a thread moved. Whoever twitched was cut.",
      marionettist: "His eyes closed and the rings of frost drew in on the cast. A cold patch opened under me. I left it early and then froze like a statue. Anyone who moved missed the cue, and was cut.",
      cleric: "Its eyes closed, and rings of frost drew in on the two young ones. A cold patch opened under one. They stepped off it early and then stood quite still. Whoever moved was cut, poor lamb.",
      grovekeeper: "Its eyes closed, and rings of frost drew in on the strikers, still as a cold morning. A patch opened under one; off it early, then not a movement. Whoever stirred was cut.",
      chronomancer: "Its eyes closed, and rings of frost drew in on the strikers. A cold patch opened under one. They stepped off early and then did not move a hair, which is the hardest rest in music. Whoever moved was cut.",
      tidecaller: "Its eyes closed, and rings of frost drew in on the strikers. A cold patch opened under one. They stepped off it early and then lay as still as slack water. Whoever moved was cut.",
      lanternkeeper: "Its eyes closed and frost rings drew in on the two strikers. A cold patch opened under one. They stepped off early and stood as still as lamp-posts, and no wick flickered. Whoever moved was cut.",
      kenseier: "Its eyes closed, and rings of frost narrowed on the strikers. A patch of cold opened under one. They stepped off on the first beat, then stood in the rest. Whoever moved was cut.",
      houndmaster: "Eyes shut. Frost rings drawing in on the pair of us, a cold patch under one. Off it early, then dead still, like standing under a bull's belly. Anyone who moved was cut.",
    } },
    "Interment": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The healer was sealed in ice. First duty: break the coffin. Then blades came for the strikers, and I left the ice to take one line, while the other went wide of theirs and straight back.",
      gloomsworn: "The healer in a block of ice, and a heavy cast ticking down beneath. We broke the coffin first. Blades went for the two strikers: I left the ice to take one line, and the other went wide and came back.",
      thresher: "Our healer was sealed in ice, and the cast beneath it ticked on. We broke the coffin before anything. Blades came for the two who strike: our shield left to take one, and the other slipped sideways, then back.",
      bloodreaver: "The healer sealed in ice, a heavy cast ticking beneath! Break the coffin first. Blades went for the hitters: I left the ice to take one, and the other jinked wide and came back.",
      runeguard: "The healer was sealed in ice, with a heavy cast beneath it: break the coffin first. Blades followed for the strikers; I left the ice for one line, while the other stepped wide and returned.",
      gorgemaw: "The healer in a block of ice, a heavy cast beginning under it. We cracked the coffin first, like a lobster. Then blades for the strikers: I left the ice to take one, and the other slipped aside and came back.",
      oathbroker: "The healer was sealed in ice, a heavy cast running beneath it. We broke the coffin first, as creditors do. Blades named both strikers: I left the ice for one line; the other stepped aside, and returned to the ice.",
      ironpalm: "The healer sealed in ice. A heavy cast under it. We broke the coffin first. Blades asked both strikers. I left the ice to answer one. The other stepped wide, and returned.",
      ranger: "The healer sealed in ice, a heavy cast starting under it. Broke the coffin first. Two blade lines at us. Our shield left the ice to take one. I stepped north off the other and came back.",
      shadowblade: "The healer sealed in ice, a heavy cast beginning under it: break the coffin first. Blades at both of us. Our shield left the ice for one line. I slipped wide of the other and went straight back.",
      pyromancer: "The healer was sealed in ice, and a heavy cast ticked beneath it. I burned at the coffin first! Then the blades came for the strikers: our shield left the ice for one line and I leapt wide of the other and went straight back.",
      thermist: "The healer sealed in ice, a heavy cast beneath it. I burned at the coffin first. Blades came for me and the other striker. Our shield left to take one line; I stepped wide of mine, hot, and was back at the ice.",
      driftblade: "The healer was sealed in ice and a heavy cast began beneath, so we broke the coffin first, and then the blades came for us and our shield left the ice to take one line while I ran wide of mine and straight back.",
      alembist: "I was sealed in ice, a heavy cast curdling beneath. They cracked the coffin first, the only sensible order. Blades for the strikers: our shield left the ice for one line, and the other sidestepped the second and returned to the glass.",
      threadweaver: "I was sealed in ice, a heavy cast beneath it. They broke the coffin first, bless them. Blades came for my needles: our shield left the ice for one line, and the other jumped the seam and came back.",
      marionettist: "The healer sealed in ice, a heavy cast beneath, and the company broke the coffin first. Blades came for the cast: the shield left the ice for one line, and I stepped aside from mine and returned to the ice.",
      cleric: "I was sealed in ice, and a heavy cast began on the coffin. They broke it before anything else, gratefully for me. Blades came for the young ones: our knight left me for one line, and the other went wide and came straight back.",
      grovekeeper: "I was sealed in ice, a heavy cast beneath it, like a seed in frozen earth. My lot broke the coffin first. Blades came for the strikers: our shield left to take one line, and the other stepped aside and came back.",
      chronomancer: "I was sealed in ice, and the cast beneath it counted down. They broke the coffin first. Blades came for the strikers: our shield left to take one, and the other sidestepped the second line and was back in time.",
      tidecaller: "I was sealed in ice, and a heavy cast began beneath, a long cold wait. The others broke the coffin first. Blades came for the strikers: our shield left the ice for one line, and the other drifted wide of the second, then back.",
      lanternkeeper: "I was sealed in ice, and the cast beneath it began. They broke the coffin first. Blades came for the strikers: our shield left the ice for one line, and the other stepped wide of the second and went straight back to my lantern.",
      kenseier: "The healer in a block of ice, a heavy cast under it. We broke the coffin first. Blades for the strikers: I left the ice to meet one, and the other stepped wide of the second line and returned.",
      houndmaster: "Healer shut in ice, heavy cast beneath. Broke the coffin first. Blades for the two of us: the shield-man left the ice for one, and I stepped wide of the other and went straight back to the ice.",
    } },
    "Two Hands": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Both hands were up: blades for the strikers, bell for the healer. I took one dash on the shield. The second striker left their line for the blue ring and stood the first toll. Nobody could do everything, so we did what mattered.",
      gloomsworn: "Blade and bell together. I took one dash. The second striker stood the toll in the blue ring beside the healer. Nobody could cover everything. The healer carried on through the last of it.",
      thresher: "Blade and bell together, dear. Our shield took the one dash. The other of us slid off their line to stand in the blue ring for a toll. Nobody could do all of it, and nobody had to.",
      bloodreaver: "Blade and bell at once. I took one dash on the chest. The other hitter left their line for the blue ring and took a toll. Nobody covered all of it. The healer held the rest together.",
      runeguard: "Both hands, and two matters at once: blades for the strikers, bell for the healer. I accepted one dash. The other striker quitted their line for the blue ring and took a toll. No order covers every part.",
      gorgemaw: "Blade and bell on one tray. I took one dash. The other striker slid out of their line into the blue ring and took a toll. Nobody covered everything. The healer finished what was left.",
      oathbroker: "Two obligations in one hour: blades for the strikers, bell for the healer. I accepted one dash. The other striker left their line for the blue ring and stood a toll. No party covered everything.",
      ironpalm: "Two voices at once, blade and bell. I answered one dash. The other striker left their line for the blue ring and answered a toll. No one answered everything. The healer answered the rest.",
      ranger: "Blade and bell. Our shield took the east dash. I went off my own line to the blue ring by the healer, took a toll, no more. Healer covered the rest.",
      shadowblade: "Blade and bell together. Our shield took one dash. I slipped off my own line and into the blue ring, for a toll. Nobody covered everything, and the healer finished the rest.",
      pyromancer: "Blade and bell at once! Our shield took one dash, and I stepped off my line into the blue ring and took a toll, dramatically. Nobody could cover everything, so the healer did the rest.",
      thermist: "Blade and bell at once. Our shield took one dash; I slid off mine and into the blue ring at the healer's side, and took a toll, cold to the bone. Nobody covered everything. Too far, almost.",
      driftblade: "Blade and bell together, and our shield took one dash, and I swung off my line into the blue ring beside the healer for a toll and out again, and nobody could cover all of it, so the healer did what was left.",
      alembist: "Two ailments in one flask: blades for the strikers, bell for me. Our shield took one dash. The other striker slid out of their line to stand in the blue ring for a toll. I brewed what was left.",
      threadweaver: "Blade and bell, two threads at once. Our shield took one dash. The other needle slipped its line for the blue ring beside me and took a toll. Nothing covers everything, so I covered the worst.",
      marionettist: "Blade and bell at once, two scenes on one stage. The shield took one dash. I slipped off my line to stand in the blue ring and take a toll. Nobody could play every part. The healer finished the scene.",
      cleric: "Blade and bell together. Our knight took one dash. The other young one slipped off their line into the blue ring beside me and took a toll. Nobody could cover everything. I mended what was left.",
      grovekeeper: "Blade and bell, like a gale and a hailstorm together. Our shield took one dash. The other striker left their line for the blue ring and took a toll. Nobody could cover everything. I tended the rest.",
      chronomancer: "Blade and bell at once, two rhythms laid on top of each other. Our shield took one dash. The other striker left their line for the blue ring and took the toll. I mended in the gaps between.",
      tidecaller: "Blade and bell together, two tides meeting. Our shield took one dash. The other striker slipped off their line into the blue ring and took a toll. Nobody could cover everything. I filled in the rest.",
      lanternkeeper: "Blade and bell together. Our shield took one dash. The other striker slipped off their line into the blue ring beside me and took a toll. Not enough lights for all of it, so I lit the ones that mattered.",
      kenseier: "Blade and bell on one count. I took a dash. The other striker slipped their line into the blue ring and took a toll. No blade covers all of it. The healer finished what was left.",
      houndmaster: "Blade and bell at once. The shield-man took one dash. I slid off mine into the blue ring by the healer and took a toll. Nobody covered all of it. The healer did the rest.",
    } },
    "Communion": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A blue ring opened round the healer and a column came down. Shared by all inside, it was a cold scare; alone it would have killed. All of us stood inside, shoulder to shoulder, and none was left out.",
      gloomsworn: "A blue ring round the healer and a column through it. Shared by all inside, a scare; alone, a grave. We all stood inside it. I have been in worse company.",
      thresher: "A blue ring round the healer, and a column through it. Shared by everyone inside, it was only a fright; alone, it would be an appointment. All four of us stood in the ring.",
      bloodreaver: "A blue ring on the healer and a column through it. Together, a scare. Alone, it kills you. All four of us in the ring, crowded as a tavern bench, and it was the best bruise of the night.",
      runeguard: "A blue ring about the healer, and a column through it. Shared by all within, a fright; alone, a death. The ring was the whole of the answer. All four of us stood inside.",
      gorgemaw: "A blue ring round the healer and a column through it. Shared among everyone inside, a nibble; alone, a feast of one. All four of us stood inside, elbow to elbow.",
      oathbroker: "A blue ring about the healer and a column through it. Shared among all inside, only a fright; borne alone, a default. All four of us stood within the ring, as the contract implies.",
      ironpalm: "A blue ring round the healer, and a column through it. Shared, a question. Alone, an end. All four of us stood inside and listened together.",
      ranger: "A blue ring round the healer, and a column dropped through it. Shared among all inside, it scared. Alone, it kills. All four of us crowded in. No line, no angle: just stand.",
      shadowblade: "A blue ring round the healer, and a column through it. Shared, a scare. Alone, a funeral. We all stood inside, shoulder to shoulder, and not one of us enjoyed it.",
      pyromancer: "A blue ring on the healer and a column dropping through it. Shared, a scare. Alone, a tragedy. All four of us stood inside, close enough to see each other's faces, and not one of us ran.",
      thermist: "A blue ring round the healer and a column through it. Together, a scare. Alone, it kills. All four of us inside, close, cold and calm, and it passed.",
      driftblade: "A blue ring round the healer and a column dropping through it, shared a scare, alone a funeral, so for once I stood in a crowd, all four of us inside, with nowhere to run and no wish to.",
      alembist: "A blue ring round me and a column through it. Shared among all inside, a scare; alone, a spill. All four of us stood in the ring, corked in together.",
      threadweaver: "A blue ring round me and a column dropping through it. Shared among all inside, a fright; alone, a snap. The four of us stood together in the ring, tied close.",
      marionettist: "A blue ring round the healer and a column through it. Shared by the company, a fright; alone, a tragedy. All four of us stood inside, downstage, close together. (The Doll applauded.)",
      cleric: "A blue ring opened round me and a column dropped through it. Shared among all inside, only a fright; alone, it would have been the end. We all stood together in the ring, which is how it should be.",
      grovekeeper: "A blue ring opened round me and a column dropped through it, like lightning into a stand of trees. Shared, only a fright; alone, a felling. All four of us stood in the ring.",
      chronomancer: "A blue ring opened round me and a column dropped through it. Shared, only a fright; alone, it would have killed. All four of us stood inside, and the beat passed over us.",
      tidecaller: "A blue ring opened round me and a column dropped through it, a great wave on a small boat. Shared among all inside, it was a spray; alone, it would have sunk us. All four of us stood in the ring.",
      lanternkeeper: "A blue ring round me and a column through it. Shared by everyone inside, a scare; alone, the lights go out. All four of us stood in the ring, close as a row of lamps.",
      kenseier: "A blue ring round the healer, and a column through it. Shared by everyone inside, a scare. Alone, a death. We all stood inside it, and the beat passed over us.",
      houndmaster: "Blue ring round the healer, column through it. Shared by all inside, a scare. Alone, it kills. All four of us stood in the ring, dogs between our boots.",
    } },
    "Verdict": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The waltz came twice, the second starting on the light, and then the verdict for all four of us. A cut in the second waltz left you frozen through it. We gave the cones room, and our healer had every one of us above half. Line stood.",
      gloomsworn: "The waltz twice, then the verdict on all four. Anyone cut in the second waltz stayed frozen through it. We gave the cones room, and the healer lifted each of us above half.",
      thresher: "The waltz twice, and then his verdict on all four of us. Anyone cut in the second dance stayed stiff for it. We kept clear of the cones, and the healer had everyone past half by the end.",
      bloodreaver: "The waltz twice, then the verdict on all four. Cut in the second waltz and you're frozen for it. I dodged the cones; the healer lifted us above half. The verdict hurt, and I was grateful for it.",
      runeguard: "The waltz twice, then the verdict upon all four. Anyone cut in the second waltz stays frozen through it. We kept from the cones, and the healer raised each of us above half before the end.",
      gorgemaw: "Two helpings of the waltz, the second starting on the light, then the last course, served to all four at once. Anyone cut in the second helping stayed frozen for it. We left every cone untouched, and the healer had us above half before the bill.",
      oathbroker: "The waltz twice, then the verdict on all four. Any party cut in the second waltz stayed frozen through it. We kept clear of the cones, and the healer had everyone above half. Settled in full.",
      ironpalm: "The waltz twice, then the verdict on all four. Cut in the second waltz, and you stay frozen through it. We kept out of the cones, and the healer had us above half. It spoke, and we were ready.",
      ranger: "Two waltzes, back to back. Held to the north rim of each cone's reach. Then the verdict, all four, and anyone cut in the second was still frozen for it.",
      shadowblade: "A pair of waltzes, the second beginning on the light, and then its verdict, which is rude to deliver to four people at once. Anyone cut in the second stays frozen. I slipped the cones, and the healer saw to the rest.",
      pyromancer: "Two waltzes, the second starting on the light, then the verdict on all four of us. Cut in the second waltz and you stay frozen through it. I danced clear of every cone, and the healer brought us above half in time.",
      thermist: "Two waltzes, back to back, the second starting on the light. I stayed clear of each cone, cold and precise, and the healer had me above half when the verdict fell. Cut in the second waltz and you are frozen through it.",
      driftblade: "Two waltzes, the second beginning on the light, and then the verdict on all four, and anyone cut in the second waltz stayed frozen through it, so I ran clear of every cone and the healer had us above half by the time it fell.",
      alembist: "Two waltzes, the second beginning on the light, then the verdict, one fixed dose for all four. Anyone cut in the second waltz stays frozen through it. Everyone must be past half on the shelf when it lands. We were.",
      threadweaver: "Two waltzes, the second starting on the light, then the verdict across all four. Anyone cut in the second waltz stays pinned through it. We cleared every cone, and I tied each of us back above half before it fell.",
      marionettist: "Two waltzes, the second entering on the light, then the verdict on the whole house. Anyone cut in the second waltz stays frozen through it. The company cleared every cone, and the healer had us past half by curtain.",
      cleric: "The waltz twice over, and then the verdict on all four. Anyone cut in the second waltz stayed frozen through it. We stepped clear of every cone, and I brought each of us above half before it fell.",
      grovekeeper: "The waltz twice over, then the verdict on all four, like two storms and a frost. Anyone cut in the second waltz stayed frozen through it. We gave the cones room, and I had everyone above half beforehand.",
      chronomancer: "Two waltzes, the second on the light, then the verdict on all four. Anyone cut in the second stayed frozen for it. We stepped clear of every cone, and I had everyone above half long before it fell.",
      tidecaller: "Two waltzes, the second starting on the light, then the verdict. Anyone cut in the second stayed frozen for it. We kept out of the cones, and I brought the water up until every one of us was above half when it broke.",
      lanternkeeper: "The waltz twice, the second starting on the light, then the verdict on all four. Anyone cut in the second stayed frozen. We kept out of every cone, and I trimmed every wick above half before it fell.",
      kenseier: "Two waltzes, the second starting on the light, then the verdict on all four. Any cut in the second waltz stays frozen for it. We stepped clear of every cone, and the healer had us above half before the last stroke. It kept its time.",
      houndmaster: "Waltz twice, second one starting on the light. Then the verdict on the four of us. Cut in the second and you stay frozen. Walked wide of every cone, with the dogs. The healer had us past half.",
    } },
    "Verdict Eternal": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "At the last it stopped waiting and raised both hands. No ground would hold against that. The only answer was to have it down before then, so we pressed it hard from the first and wasted no time.",
      gloomsworn: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands, and nothing we had would stand against it. The only answer was to be finished before then.",
      thresher: "At the end he stopped waiting and raised both hands, and that, dear, is an hour even I could not hurry or delay. The thing to do was be finished before it. We were quick, and it was lovely.",
      bloodreaver: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands. Nothing to hit back at. Be done before that, my friend, and hit harder from the start.",
      runeguard: "It stopped waiting and raised both hands, and no ward would hold. This one cannot be foreseen, only outrun: we must be finished before it, and so we pressed it hard from the first.",
      gorgemaw: "At the end he stopped waiting and raised both hands: the bill, and no one could pay it. We had to leave before it came, so we ate fast and early and did not stop.",
      oathbroker: "At the last it stopped waiting and raised both hands, and no clause would answer. The only remedy was to conclude before then, so we struck early and without pause.",
      ironpalm: "In the end it stopped asking and raised both hands. There was nothing to answer. We finished it before it spoke again, and did not rest.",
      ranger: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands. No way round it. The only shot is to finish it first, and fast.",
      shadowblade: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands. Nothing to slip behind. The only way out was to finish it first, so we struck early and did not stop.",
      pyromancer: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands, and I was not in the mood to find out what comes next. We must be done before then, so I started my best spells early and did not stop.",
      thermist: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands. Too far, even for me. Be finished before then, and burn hot and early.",
      driftblade: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands, and there was no gap left to slip through, so we had to be finished before then, and we struck early and fast and without a pause.",
      alembist: "At the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands. No remedy for that. The only prescription was to be finished before, so we struck early and I brewed fast.",
      threadweaver: "At the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands, and no seam would hold. The only answer was to be finished before then, so we struck early and I worked fast.",
      marionettist: "At the end the star stopped waiting and raised both hands. No cue followed. We had to be done before then: the company struck early and without pause.",
      cleric: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands, and no prayer would turn it. The kindest thing was to finish it before then, so we struck early, and my friends did not tire.",
      grovekeeper: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands, and it was the hardest winter I have read. The only answer was to be done before it came. We struck early and steadily, as you reap before the frost.",
      chronomancer: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands. There is no beat after that. We had to be finished before then, so we struck early and I undid what I could.",
      tidecaller: "In the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands, and no sea has ever turned back from that. The only answer was to be finished before it rose, so we struck early and kept on.",
      lanternkeeper: "At the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands, and there was no oil left in the world for that. We had to be finished before it, so we struck early and I kept the wicks high.",
      kenseier: "At the end it stopped waiting and raised both hands. That is a blow with no rest after it. A blade does not turn it. We had to be done before then, and so we pressed from the first stroke.",
      houndmaster: "In the end he stopped waiting and raised both hands. Nowhere to run. Had to be done before then, so we went in early and did not stop.",
    } },
  },
};
